.Dd October 16, 2026
.Dt LCC-WALLPAPER 1
.Os @PROJECT_VERSION@

.Sh NAME
.Nm lcc-wallpaper
.Nd configure Lumina desktop background images.

.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h | -help
.Op Fl v | -version
.Op Fl s | -screen Ar screen

.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is part of the Lumina Control Center.
It sets the background for one screen and shows a preview along with the
screen resolution.
Backgrounds can be single images, whole directories of images, or solid
colors, and the layout of the image on the screen can be chosen.
When more than one background is configured, they can be rotated
automatically at a set interval in minutes.

.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Display help on command line options.
.It Fl v , Fl -version
Display version information.
.It Fl s Ar screen , Fl -screen Ar screen
Show the configuration for screen number
.Ar screen ,
counted from 0.
The default is 0.
An invalid screen number is ignored and screen 0 is used.
.El

.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl % lcc-wallpaper --screen 1
Configure the background of the second monitor.

.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /usr/local/bin/lcc-wallpaper
.It Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lumina-desktop/desktopsettings.conf
Background settings shared with
.Xr lumina-desktop 1 .
.El

.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lcc 1 ,
.Xr lcc-desktop 1 ,
.Xr lumina-desktop 1

